-- Boot smoke test for this package.
--
-- Asserts register_with_config returns without runtime panic. Catches
-- the class of bugs that pass `ailang check` but crash at runtime:
--
--   - Pattern matches against the wrong ADT (e.g. matching Result
--     constructors against an Option value — std/json.getString
--     returns Option, not Result; the original 0.1.1 code had this bug
--     and it took the consumer (motoko_agent) crashing on first turn
--     to find it)
--   - readFile-style panics when defaults aren't present
--   - Cross-package ADT shape drift (variants added/removed in deps)
--
-- The cfg param is `_cfg: a` (generic, unused) in this package's
-- register_with_config — pass any value; the package ignores it.
--
-- Convention: every motoko-ext-* package SHOULD ship a _smoke.ail
-- with this exact shape. The parent Makefile :: verify-extensions
-- iterates over packages/motoko-ext-* and runs each _smoke.ail in
-- isolation (process-per-package, so a panic in pkg A doesn't mask
-- pkg B's status). New packages without _smoke.ail get a warning
-- but don't fail the build (yet) — promote to error once all
-- existing packages have one.
module sunholo/motoko_ext_compaction_ai/_smoke

import std/io (println)
import pkg/sunholo/motoko_ext_compaction_ai/register (register_with_config)

export func main() -> () ! {Env, FS, IO} {
  let _ = register_with_config(0);
  println("OK: register_with_config returned without panic")
}
